# Local development configuration for astro-server
# Usage: cp .env.example .env && go run main.go
#
# Setup:
#   1. Docker Desktop with Kubernetes enabled (Settings > Kubernetes > Enable
#   2. Start with moon run astro-server:dev

# Database. The dev database is remote: set this to your dev DB connection
# string (ask the team for the shared dev DB URL). There is no local Postgres.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@DEV_DB_HOST:5432/astro?sslmode=require

# Kubernetes: use local kubeconfig instead of EKS/IRSA
K8S_CLIENT_MODE=local
KUBE_CONTEXT=docker-desktop
REGISTRY_URL=docker.io/library
ENVIRONMENT=local

# Auth — use stage WorkOS credentials for local dev
WORKOS_API_KEY=sk_test_...
WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=client_...
AUTH_COOKIE_PASSWORD=VTDXE7UIxD3+54UxkX1yl7SQNVXp3/j4PH69va/tEuE=
# Compare legacy deployment authorization with WorkOS without enforcing it.
# FGA_SHADOW_ENABLED=true
# Enforce reviewed mutations for opted-in, FGA-ready organization deployments.
# FGA_ENFORCEMENT_ENABLED=true

# Server
PORT=8080
ADMIN_GRPC_PORT=9091
GIN_MODE=release
LOG_LEVEL=debug
SERVER_MODE=api

# Avatars / assets — use the repo-root assets/ dir as a local filesystem store.
# The server mounts a static file handler at /assets/ when ASSETS_LOCAL_DIR is set,
# so ASSETS_CDN_URL must match the path the handler is mounted at.
ASSETS_LOCAL_DIR=../../assets
ASSETS_CDN_URL=http://localhost:8080/assets

# Loki — use Adhoc Loki for local dev
LOKI_URL=https://loki.adhoc.dev.astropod.ai

# Prometheus — use Adhoc Prometheus for local dev
PROMETHEUS_URL=https://prometheus.adhoc.dev.astropod.ai

# AI Gateway — LiteLLM proxy for managed model access (provider: astro-gateway).
# Leave both unset to disable the feature locally — specs using
# provider:astro-gateway will then be rejected by the validator with a clear
# error. To test end-to-end against the real gateway, point at the preview
# env's public hostname and grab the master key from AWS Secrets Manager
# (astro/ai-gateway/preview/master-key).
AI_GATEWAY_URL=https://aig.astropod.ai
AI_GATEWAY_ADMIN_URL=https://admin.aig.astropod.ai
AI_GATEWAY_ADMIN_AUTH=Basic ...

# Langfuse — observability backend for agent traces
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://langfuse.adhoc.dev.astropod.ai
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL_EXT — external Langfuse URL passed to collector (overrides LANGFUSE_BASE_URL when set)
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL_EXT=https://langfuse.ext.astropod.ai
# LANGFUSE_VPCE_IPS — comma-separated VPC endpoint IPs for Langfuse PrivateLink (added to NetworkPolicy egress)
# LANGFUSE_VPCE_IPS=10.3.11.50,10.3.12.50
LANGFUSE_DB_URL=postgres://...
LANGFUSE_SALT=...
LANGFUSE_ORG_ID=astro

# OTel ingest — public URL rendered into the managed-settings block on the Data
# Sources page. Point at a locally-run astro-otel to collect Claude Code
# telemetry from your own machine.
OTEL_INGEST_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# Foundry work-classifier — labels Claude Code prompts by purpose and topic.
# Both must be set together or startup fails; leave both blank to disable
# classification entirely (the workers no-op).
#
# Deliberately blank: the classifier runs on a shared inference pool and the
# discovery job fires on startup, so a copied-in default would point local dev
# at production capacity. Endpoint is https://inference.foundry.astroids.ai.
# Look the version up in astro-infra (work_classifier_versions in
# terraform/environments/foundry/terraform.tfvars) rather than copying a pin
# from here — a stale value means a retrained model is served under the old
# stamp and nothing is ever re-classified.
FOUNDRY_INFERENCE_URL=
WORK_CLASSIFIER_VERSION=

# GitHub repo connection — automated builds
# GITHUB_CALLBACK_URL — public base URL for OAuth callbacks and webhook delivery.
# Use an ngrok tunnel in local dev: ngrok http 8080, then set to https://xxx.ngrok-free.app
# Falls back to FRONTEND_URL if not set.
# GITHUB_CALLBACK_URL=https://xxx.ngrok-free.app

# Supabase OAuth integration — project auto-import for PostgreSQL knowledge stores.
# OAuth is brokered by WorkOS Pipes as a custom provider (slug "supabase"), so
# there are NO Supabase env vars here: WorkOS holds the client credentials and
# stores/refreshes the tokens. Configure the custom provider in the WorkOS
# dashboard (authorize https://api.supabase.com/v1/oauth/authorize, token
# https://api.supabase.com/v1/oauth/token) and set its redirect URI to WorkOS's
# callback. Requires WORKOS_API_KEY (already set above for auth).

# Billing — hosted metering (Metronome) + card vault (Stripe). All optional;
# leave unset for local dev (billing defaults to the no-op provider). Stripe only
# collects/saves a card via SetupIntent; Metronome charges the saved card.
# BILLING_PROVIDER=metronome
# METRONOME_API_KEY=...
# METRONOME_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...
# Signup provisioning. Without a package id no contract is created, so nothing
# draws down and the exhaustion gate never engages. The package carries the
# signup credit, so its amount, unit, and expiry are configured in Metronome.
# METRONOME_PACKAGE_ID=...
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
